# Technical Design Document: chat-frontend-ui-redesign

## 1) Architecture Overview (React + Zustand + React Query + Socket.IO)

**Goal**: Redesign the chat UI (“Alt A — Industrial Quiet”: Zinc neutrals, Emerald accent, status-first, no glow) while keeping data correctness and realtime behavior deterministic.

**Runtime stack**
- **React 19**: UI rendering + concurrent rendering safety (no side-effectful render logic).
- **Zustand**: **ephemeral UI + realtime presence** state (selected chat, connection, typing map, toast queue).
- **React Query**: **server state** (chats, messages, notifications) with optimistic updates + cache patching from WS.
- **Socket.IO client**: realtime events; joins/leaves chat rooms based on selection; auth via JWT.

**Layering (strict boundaries)**
- `features/*/api/*`: HTTP clients (React Query fetchers) only.
- `features/realtime/*`: socket client + event router only (no JSX).
- `features/*/store/*`: Zustand stores only (no network).
- `features/*/containers/*`: data wiring (RQ + Zustand + socket), no styling decisions.
- `features/*/components/*`: presentational (pure props), Tailwind classes only.

**Existing server WS contract (must match)**
- inbound: `joinChat(chatId)`, `leaveChat(chatId)`
- outbound: `message`, `typing`, `notification`

## 2) Component Tree (Strict boundaries, container-presentational)

```
<AppShellContainer>
  <AppShell> (layout, chrome)
    <ChatPageContainer>
      <ChatLayout> (2/3-column responsive grid, status-first header)
        <ChatListContainer>
          <ChatList> (presentational)
            <ChatListItem />
        <ChatThreadContainer>
          <ChatThreadHeader /> (status + metadata, no glow)
          <MessageListContainer>
            <MessageList>
              <MessageBubble />
              <TypingIndicator />
          <MessageComposerContainer>
            <MessageComposer />
        <NotificationTrayContainer> (optional)
          <NotificationTray />
```

**Container responsibilities**
- Fetch via React Query, call mutations, subscribe/unsubscribe to socket rooms, patch caches, translate domain → view models.
- Read/write Zustand for ephemeral state (selection, typing, connection).

**Presentational responsibilities**
- Render props, emit UI events (`onSelectChat`, `onSend`, `onRetry`).
- No direct store access, no `useQuery`, no socket calls.

## 3) State Flow (How WS events update the Zustand/RQ store)

**Sources of truth**
- **Server state**: React Query caches
  - `['chats']` (infinite)
  - `['messages', chatId]` (infinite)
  - `['notifications']`
- **Ephemeral state**: Zustand
  - `selectedChatId`
  - `socket.status` (`disconnected|connecting|connected|error`)
  - `typingByChatId: Record<chatId, Set<userId>>` with TTL eviction
  - `toasts[]` (status-first feedback)

**Connection + room membership**
1. `AuthStore.token` (persisted) is provided in Socket.IO handshake (`auth.token`).
2. `selectedChatId` changes:
   - emit `leaveChat(prevChatId)` (if any)
   - emit `joinChat(nextChatId)`
   - optionally prefetch `['messages', nextChatId]`

**WS → cache/store patching (single event router)**
- `socket.on('message', msg)`:
  - `queryClient.setQueryData(['messages', msg.chatId], patchInfiniteAddNewest(msg))`
  - `queryClient.setQueryData(['chats'], patchChatPreview(msg.chatId, msg.content, msg.createdAt))`
  - clear typing state for that sender in `typingByChatId[msg.chatId]`
- `socket.on('typing', {chatId, userId})`:
  - `chatUIStore.setTyping(chatId, userId, ttlMs=3000)`
  - no React Query changes (ephemeral)
- `socket.on('notification', notif)`:
  - `queryClient.setQueryData(['notifications'], prependNotification(notif))`
  - `chatUIStore.enqueueToast({kind:'info', title:notif.title})`

**HTTP mutation → optimistic + WS reconciliation**
- Send message:
  - optimistic insert to `['messages', chatId]` with temp id
  - on success: keep; on error: mark failed + surface status-first toast
  - when WS `message` arrives: de-dup by `(chatId, senderId, createdAt/content)` or server id once available

## 4) Tailwind v4 Design Tokens (OKLCH palette, typography)

**Token strategy**
- Tailwind v4 **CSS-first tokens**: define OKLCH variables once; use semantic tokens everywhere (`--color-surface`, `--color-accent`, `--color-danger`).
- “No glow”: avoid `ring-*` glow patterns; use `outline` + subtle border contrast.

```css
/* src/styles/theme.css */
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  /* Neutrals — Zinc-like, Industrial Quiet */
  --color-bg: oklch(0.985 0.005 270);
  --color-surface: oklch(0.965 0.007 270);
  --color-surface-2: oklch(0.935 0.010 270);
  --color-border: oklch(0.870 0.012 270);
  --color-text: oklch(0.220 0.020 270);
  --color-muted: oklch(0.520 0.020 270);

  /* Accent — Emerald, restrained */
  --color-accent: oklch(0.700 0.140 160);
  --color-accent-2: oklch(0.620 0.120 160);
  --color-accent-ink: oklch(0.160 0.030 160);

  /* Status-first */
  --color-success: oklch(0.720 0.150 155);
  --color-warning: oklch(0.780 0.140 85);
  --color-danger: oklch(0.650 0.190 25);
  --color-info: oklch(0.700 0.070 240);

  /* Typography */
  --font-sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Inter, Arial;
  --text-xs: 0.75rem;
  --text-sm: 0.875rem;
  --text-base: 1rem;
  --text-lg: 1.125rem;

  /* Shape + elevation (quiet) */
  --radius-sm: 0.5rem;
  --radius-md: 0.75rem;
  --shadow-quiet: 0 1px 0 oklch(0 0 0 / 0.06), 0 8px 24px oklch(0 0 0 / 0.08);
}

/* Focus: outline, not glow */
:where(button, a, input, textarea):focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

**Usage rules (enforced)**
- Surfaces: `bg-[--color-bg]`, `bg-[--color-surface]`; borders always visible (`border-[--color-border]`).
- Accent only for primary actions + selected state (no blue).
- Status components lead with icon + label + color token; avoid decorative effects.
